From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: opencode <opencode@localhost>
Date: Fri, 02 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [Bugfix] Key the AOT compile cache on limit_mm_per_prompt
 (upstream #50891)

Version-locked to VLLM_REF=v0.31.0. Upstream issue #50891 (open, no
fix PR): ModelConfig.compute_hash() lists `limit_mm_per_prompt` in
ignored_factors, so serving the same model with different image caps
(e.g. image:0 vs image:99) collides on one torch-compile cache entry
and crashes in profile_run (`AttributeError: 'NoneType' object has no
attribute 'size'`). The mismatch is bidirectional and guard checking is
disabled on cache hit, so a poisoned artifact can break a previously
working deployment in either direction.

Minimal variant: only the caps are keyed (as a structural
MultiModalDummyOptions normalization — verified deterministic), leaving
`multimodal_config` itself ignored. Subtlety that shaped this form:
ModelConfig takes `limit_mm_per_prompt` as an InitVar, which is not a
dataclass field and is never retained on the instance (it is folded
into MultiModalConfig.limit_per_prompt at construction) — so merely
dropping it from ignored_factors is a silent no-op (verified: hashes
still collided). The fix keys the folded value explicitly. One-time
effect on adoption: existing compile-cache entries are invalidated and
rebuilt once (key change only, no runtime behavior change).

Not currently exposed here (all qwen3.8-27b runs share image cap 99 —
see the #50891 hygiene rule in AGENTS.md); carried as insurance and as
an upstreamable fix. Drop when a pinned VLLM_REF keys the compile cache
on the multimodal config.
---
diff --git a/vllm/config/model.py b/vllm/config/model.py
index 15d046de7..5ed25002b 100644
--- a/vllm/config/model.py
+++ b/vllm/config/model.py
@@ -456,7 +456,6 @@ class ModelConfig:
             "io_processor_plugin",
             "pooler_config",
             "multimodal_config",
-            "limit_mm_per_prompt",
             "media_io_kwargs",
             "mm_processor_kwargs",
             "mm_processor_cache_gb",
@@ -468,7 +467,11 @@ class ModelConfig:
             "mm_ipc_gpu_memory_gb",
         }

-        from vllm.config.utils import get_hash_factors, hash_factors
+        from vllm.config.utils import (
+            get_hash_factors,
+            hash_factors,
+            normalize_value,
+        )

         factors = get_hash_factors(self, ignored_factors)

@@ -477,6 +480,14 @@ class ModelConfig:
         # here early.
         if self.multimodal_config:
             factors["language_model_only"] = self.multimodal_config.language_model_only
+            # The per-prompt multimodal caps change the model's forward
+            # signature (image-capable vs text-only graphs compile
+            # differently), so they must key the compile cache (upstream
+            # #50891). ModelConfig takes the caps as an InitVar, which is
+            # not a dataclass field, so key the folded value explicitly.
+            factors["limit_per_prompt"] = normalize_value(
+                self.multimodal_config.limit_per_prompt
+            )
         return hash_factors(factors)

     def _update_nested(
